---
// PlansTeaser.astro: pilot-first offer for each side of the bridge.
---
<section class="section plans-t on-paper-2" aria-labelledby="plans-t-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head section-head--split">
      <p class="eyebrow">07 · Plans</p>
      <h2 id="plans-t-title" class="h2">Start with a pilot on <em>your own</em> tenders.</h2>
      <p class="lead">No slideware. We prove Kriseva on your work first, then quote for the modules, deployment and team you actually need.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="plans-t__grid rv-stagger">
      <article class="pt-card">
        <p class="mono pt-card__k">For suppliers · TAS</p>
        <h3 class="pt-card__t">TAS pilot</h3>
        <p class="pt-card__d">We set TAS up on your machine, load your capability list, and run it on live tenders with your bid team.</p>
        <ul role="list" class="pt-card__list">
          <li>Your portals, your keywords, your capability list</li>
          <li>Daily shortlist with bid, review or skip reasons</li>
          <li>Runs on your own machine</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact?intent=pilot&amp;side=supplier">Request a TAS pilot <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="pt-card">
        <p class="mono pt-card__k">For buyers · Evaluator</p>
        <h3 class="pt-card__t">Evaluator sandbox</h3>
        <p class="pt-card__d">One closed tender, in your room. We run Evaluator on a tender your committee has already decided, so you can check every finding against your own result.</p>
        <ul role="list" class="pt-card__list">
          <li>A known result to check us against</li>
          <li>Every finding linked to its page</li>
          <li>Offline, on your premises</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact?intent=pilot&amp;side=buyer">Request a sandbox <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>
      <a class="pt-card pt-card--quote" href="/plans">
        <p class="mono pt-card__k">Custom quote</p>
        <h3 class="pt-card__t">Build your plan</h3>
        <p class="pt-card__d">Pick a side, the modules and the deployment. Your request goes straight to the founder.</p>
        <span class="link-arrow">Open the plan builder <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .plans-t__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(0.85rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
  }

  .pt-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 1rem + 1.4vw, 2.2rem);
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .pt-card__k {
    color: var(--brass-ink);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
  }

  .pt-card__t {
    font-family: var(--f-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 1.2rem + 1vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .pt-card__d {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: var(--t-small);
  }

  .pt-card__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--t-small);
  }

  .pt-card__list li {
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .pt-card__list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--brass);
  }

  .pt-card .btn {
    margin-top: auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  .pt-card--quote {
    background: var(--navy);
    color: var(--on-navy);
    border-color: var(--navy);
    transition: transform 0.4s var(--ease);
  }

  .pt-card--quote:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }

  .pt-card--quote .pt-card__k,
  .pt-card--quote .link-arrow {
    color: var(--brass-light);
  }

  .pt-card--quote .pt-card__d {
    color: var(--on-navy-2);
  }

  .pt-card--quote .link-arrow {
    margin-top: auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  @media (width <= 980px) {
    .plans-t__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
